### **1. Infosys and Carlos Alcaraz Partner to Launch Generative AI Performance Tools**
*   **Published:** April 15, 2026
*   **Source:** Stock Titan / Firstpost
*   **URL:** [https://www.stocktitan.net/news/INFY/7-time-grand-slam-champion-carlos-alcaraz-is-infosys-global-brand-nduygwsk3ttx.html](https://www.stocktitan.net/news/INFY/7-time-grand-slam-champion-carlos-alcaraz-is-infosys-global-brand-nduygwsk3ttx.html)
*   **Article Content:**
    Infosys has announced a multi-year global partnership with seven-time Grand Slam champion Carlos Alcaraz, appointing him as a brand ambassador to spearhead a new era of AI-driven tennis analytics. Beyond marketing, the collaboration focuses on the co-development of a generative AI-led "Performance Architect" toolset. This platform will utilize Infosys’s Topaz AI suite to analyze match footage and biometric data, providing Alcaraz’s coaching team with real-time strategic adjustments and predictive modeling for upcoming opponents. The partnership aims to democratize high-level coaching insights by eventually integrating these AI tools into the Infosys Tennis Platform, which serves fans and amateur players at major tournaments like Roland-Garros and the Australian Open. The initiative highlights a shift in the industry toward "athlete-centric AI," where professional players actively participate in training the models that analyze their unique physical and tactical profiles.

### **2. Orange Lion Sports Debuts Industry-First "AI Event Operations Assistant"**
*   **Published:** April 14, 2026
*   **Source:** ANTARA News
*   **URL:** [https://en.antaranews.com/news/412147/orange-lion-sports-ushers-in-sports-industrys-agent-era-with-debut-of-ai-event-operations-assistant](https://en.antaranews.com/news/412147/orange-lion-sports-ushers-in-sports-industrys-agent-era-with-debut-of-ai-event-operations-assistant)
*   **Article Content:**
    Orange Lion Sports (formerly Alibaba Sports) has unveiled a generative AI "Tournament Assistant" powered by the Qwen 3.5 model, signaling the "Agent Era" for sports administration. The tool enables "one-sentence event hosting," where users can launch a professional-grade competition by providing a single natural-language prompt (e.g., "Set up a junior tennis tournament for 200 players using ATP rules"). The AI interprets the request, generates match schedules, creates registration portals, and sets up scoring protocols in minutes—a process that traditionally takes days of manual labor. Integrated with computer vision systems at over 120 courts in China, the assistant automatically ingest live match data, verifies results against national databases (such as the Chinese Tennis Association), and generates AI-produced highlight reels for social media. This deployment demonstrates a measurable impact on operational efficiency, drastically lowering the barrier for local organizations to host sanctioned athletic events.

### **3. Fubo Rebuilds Mobile Experience with AI-Driven Live Video Analytics**
*   **Published:** April 9, 2026
*   **Source:** PPC Land
*   **URL:** [https://ppc.land/fubo-rebuilds-its-mobile-app-with-ai-for-on-the-go-sports-fans/](https://ppc.land/fubo-rebuilds-its-mobile-app-with-ai-for-on-the-go-sports-fans/)
*   **Article Content:**
    Sports-first streaming platform Fubo has launched a comprehensive update to its mobile applications, centered on a new proprietary AI engine that analyzes live broadcast signals in real-time. The update introduces "Live Video Carousels" and "Vertical Team Channels," which use computer vision to identify key moments—such as scoring chances, turnovers, or record-breaking plays—and instantly serve them as bite-sized, vertical video previews to users. Unlike traditional highlight services that require manual clipping, Fubo’s AI detects the context of the game to alert fans when a high-leverage moment is occurring (e.g., a "red zone" possession in football or a "break point" in tennis). The tool is designed to drive fan engagement by reducing "channel surfing" and ensuring users never miss critical live action. This rollout represents a significant industrial deployment of AI to solve the challenge of discoverability in the increasingly fragmented sports media landscape.